	abstract = {Guaranteeing deadline adherence for Ultra-Reliable Low-Latency Communication (URLLC) tasks in Mobile Edge Computing (MEC) requires intelligent scheduling, especially under environmental uncertainty. In this work, we address the challenge of deciding not only how, but also when, to offload tasks in the face of volatile wireless channels and fluctuating server loads. We propose a Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) framework utilizing Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO), where an agent learns to dynamically balance immediate task offloading against strategic deferral. By operating in a continuous action space with a size-invariant state representation, our agent learns a scalable policy capable of zero-shot generalization. Simulations demonstrate that the proposed PPO agent achieves a competitive task completion rate comparable to sophisticated heuristics while reducing energy consumption by approximately 20% through intelligent deferral. Furthermore, we demonstrate that PPO significantly outperforms Soft Actor-Critic (SAC) in terms of computational efficiency, training 5 × faster and avoiding the policy collapse observed in the off-policy baseline. Extensive stress tests validate the agent's robustness against network congestion and severe channel volatility, positioning it as a sustainable and deployable solution for real-time Edge Intelligence. © 2026 IEEE.},
