tal pathology; clinical trial registry records; benchmark resources; and controlled-access catalogs). The release contains normalized metadata tables, the CCDCAT schema and controlled vocabularies, provenance and query logs, an abstention ledger, and a queryable database. The CCDCAT is metadata-only: it provides stable host identifiers and resolvable landing-page references to original source records, together with access pathways and requirements, but it does not host or redistribute participant-level primary data (e.g., omics files, images, or other protected files) governed by external repositories. The DOI/link was submitted as supplementary material to this manuscript. Dataset License: CC0 1.0 Universal (applies to CCDCAT metadata and release artifacts only). Underlying source datasets remain under their original repository-specific licenses and access/governance conditions. © 2026 by the authors.},
