	abstract = {Grasshoppers are economically important insects affecting agricultural and grassland production, and accurate species-level identification is essential for pest monitoring and subsequent ecological analysis. However, automated recognition remains challenging for morphologically similar species. In this study, we constructed a standardized multi-view image dataset comprising 9128 images from 878 pinned adult grasshopper specimens representing 7 families, 28 genera, and 41 species. All images from the same specimen were assigned to the same data partition to prevent specimen-level information leakage. Based on this dataset, we developed CA-MFE-SwinT, which integrates the hierarchical shifted-window architecture of Swin Transformer with Coordinate Attention (CA) to enhance directional spatial information and a Multi-scale Morphological Feature Enhancement (MFE) module to capture morphology-related features across different spatial scales.CA-MFE-SwinT achieved a Top-1 accuracy of 92.26  ±  1.38%, a Top-3 accuracy of 97.09  ±  0.69%, and a macro-averaged F1 score of 91.47  ±  1.34% in the 41-class recognition task, outperforming all evaluated baseline models in terms of overall performance. After aggregating multi-view predictions from each specimen, specimen-level performance remained comparable to that at the image level. Ablation experiments showed that CA and MFE made complementary contributions, with their combination achieving the best performance. Further analyses indicated that misclassifications were concentrated among morphologically similar taxa, while confidence calibration and selective prediction helped identify low-confidence samples for further expert review.These results indicate that CA-MFE-SwinT enables effective fine-grained recognition of standardized adult grasshopper specimen images and can support laboratory-assisted species identification and confidence-guided candidate screening. The Author(s) This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC license. http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/},
