	abstract = {Academic procedures in universities are often complex, distributed across multiple offices, and described in heterogeneous documents, making it difficult for students to obtain accurate and timely guidance. To address this challenge, this paper proposes an ontology-driven automatic question answering (QA) system that supports Vietnamese natural-language queries about academic procedures. The system integrates a domain-specific ontology-modeled in OWL 2 to represent processes such as course registration, retake, withdrawal, academic deferral, tuition payment, scholarship review, and graduation evaluation - with modern Vietnamese NLP techniques. A hybrid pipeline is developed, combining VnCoreNLP tokenization, Sentence-BERT semantic embeddings, rule-based intent detection, and entity linking with ontology concepts. A SPARQL reasoning engine then maps detected intents to query templates and retrieves procedural information through adaptive query expansion and multi-hop inference. A prototype chatbot was implemented and evaluated on a dataset of frequently asked questions collected from Nha Trang University. Experimental results show that the proposed approach achieves 85.0% QA accuracy, outperforming keyword-based and rule-based baselines, while additional metrics such as MRR, ACS and SSS confirm its robustness in semantic understanding and answer completeness. The system demonstrates the effectiveness of combining ontology and Vietnamese NLP models to enhance academic support and promote digital transformation in higher education. © 2026 IEEE.},
