	abstract = {The growth of Bitcoin cryptocurrency with large fluctuations has aroused the interest of large investors, leading to the need for institutional investors to be at the forefront of short-term cryptocurrency trend prediction technology. To address the complexities caused by nonlinearity, this paper proposes a fusion model combining the MobileNetV2 model to capture candlestick chart morphology, OHLCV series with technical indicators modeled by GRU for short-term dependencies, and nonautoregressive encoder (NAR) to extract long-term context. Then, the features of each model are merged into the XGBoost model for classification (Bull/Bear/Neutral), which is mapped into trading signals while integrating the Uncertainty gating decision mechanism to increase reliability. Using the 15minute BTC/USDT dataset from Binance, divided into 70%/15%/15% ensembles, the merged model achieved an accuracy of 74.3 %, macro-F1 of 0.7429, and MCC of 0.4867, outperforming the single-method and baseline methods. The trust-aware gating results further improved the reliability, raising the accuracy and F1 to over 81% with a coverage of 67.74%, with a high threshold exceeding 98% accuracy for selective predictions. The above results demonstrate that the combination of multi-methods with the Uncertainty gating decision mechanism provides a reliable and practical forecasting tool for the volatile cryptocurrency market. © 2025 IEEE.},
