	abstract = {As Precision Agriculture (PA) evolves through the integration of Industry 4.0 technologies, it also faces new and sophisticated threats. This paper presents an in-depth analysis and framework for threat detection in PA utilizing Artificial Intelligence (AI). The proposed framework focuses on identifying and mitigating both cybersecurity and physical threats that could compromise the efficiency, safety, and sustainability of agricultural operations. By leveraging machine learning algorithms and real-time data analytics, the framework aims to provide proactive threat detection and response mechanisms, ensuring robust protection for PA systems. This study System describes a network threats detection mechanism using machine learning for IoT-based precision farming application. In the first phase of this research detection of http threats under the large Wireless Sensor Networks (WSN). We developed a cloud-connected precision farming application & applied the data mining & machine learning algorithms for accurate Hypertext Transfer Protocol(HTTP) threats. In this paper describes an cross-layer-based clustering & routing algorithms have been intended to diminish network correspondence deferral, dormancy, & energy utilization. The boundaries of various layers like a physical, Medium Access Control (MAC) & network layer of every sensor are utilized to assess & choose ideal Optimized Cross-Layer Routing for Industry 4.0(OCLRI) & productive information transmission. Initial cluster head (CH) selection has done and then Ant Colony Optimization (ACO) proposed for secure data transmission. In experimental analysis results demonstrates the proposed OCLRI-ACO techniques improves the overall QoS parameters. © 2024 IEEE.},
