	abstract = {We study the problem of classification with a reject option for a fixed predictor, crucial to natural language processing. We introduce a new problem formulation for this scenario, and an algorithm minimizing a new surrogate loss function. We provide a complete theoretical analysis of the surrogate loss function with a strong H-consistency guarantee. For evaluation, we choose the decontextualization task, and provide a manually-labelled dataset of 2,000 examples. Our algorithm significantly outperforms the baselines considered, with a ∼25% improvement in coverage when halving the error rate, which is only ∼3% away from the theoretical limit. © 2024 12th International Conference on Learning Representations, ICLR 2024. All rights reserved.},
